  "definition": {
    "window": "The From and To dates (YYYY-MM-DD, inclusive; all dates if none given) apply to the date the engine treated as today when each cycle ran. On a system running in real time that is the real date; in this demo's back-dated history it is the simulated date, the same clock the alerts and deadlines use. The start time shown on each row is the real wall-clock time and is not what the window selects. The status filter applies to rows and totals alike.",
    "rows": "One row per recorded engine cycle in the window, newest first, paged. Each row shows what that cycle checked, created and suppressed, and how it ended. Provenance on a row says how it was produced: TEST_RUN (automated tests), BENCHMARK (load test), SIMULATED (run on a pinned or moved clock, or run by the seed script even though the seed's last cycle uses the real clock), LIVE_DEMO (run on the real clock by something other than the seed, tests or a load test). If more than one applies, TEST_RUN outranks BENCHMARK, which outranks SIMULATED, which outranks LIVE_DEMO.",
    "totals": "Counted over every run in the window and status filter, in one query, not from the page shown: runCount = runs; failedCount = runs that ended FAILED. alertsCreated and alertsSuppressed are blank (not 0) when no run is recorded in the window, because then nothing was measured.",
    "abandoned": "A run still marked running more than 15 minutes of real elapsed time after it started is counted as abandoned, not in progress, because a crash, hard kill or out-of-memory stop cannot update its own row. abandonedCount is: of the runs in the window and status filter, those still marked running more than 15 minutes of real elapsed time after they started. A stuck run dated outside the window is not counted here; the Overview counts all dates.",
    "alertsCreated": "Alerts newly logged by the runs in the window, summed from the run records. It equals the alert-log total for the same window only when every alert was raised by a recorded run and each alert is dated the same day as its run (a cycle that crosses midnight breaks that); the two answer different questions (alerts logged vs. what runs reported).",
    "alertsSuppressed": "Duplicate alerts the runs declined to create because the alert log's unique key (item, kind, level) already held them, summed over the runs in the window. These were prevented, not delivered twice; this build has no external delivery channel."
  },
